  "title": "RAG Ingestion, Retrieval & Grounded Answers",
  "description": "A left-to-right system map showing how versioned, permission-carrying source content is ingested, normalized, classified, chunked, embedded, and atomically published across vector, document, and keyword stores. The lower lane covers quarantine, retries, dead letters, repair/rollback, and embedding-model rebuilds. The query lane rewrites questions, performs hybrid retrieval, reranks and permission-filters evidence, then produces cited grounded answers or an explicit “I don’t know”; feedback and coverage gaps loop back into ingestion priorities.",
